msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:509
msgid "The map doesn’t show"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:511
msgid "Is the page waiting for consent? Accept cookies in your consent banner, or check Settings → Privacy & consent."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:512
msgid "Caching and optimisation plugins that combine or delay JavaScript can stop maps loading. Exclude MatrixMap’s scripts (their paths contain <code>/geo-maps/build/</code>) and clear the cache."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:513
msgid "Check the Dashboard’s health card and your browser’s console for a “[MatrixMap]” message."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:515
msgid "The map is grey or has no streets"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:516
msgid "The tile or style server may be blocked by a firewall or ad blocker, or a keyed provider rejected the key. Try another style in Settings → Maps & style. The map shows a message when tiles keep failing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:517
msgid "An address isn’t found"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:518
msgid "Add the postcode and country, or type the coordinates (latitude, longitude). The free OpenStreetMap search allows about one lookup per second; heavy imports should use a keyed service (Settings → Address search). If an address changed, clear the address cache (Import & Tools → Maintenance)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:519
msgid "The store locator finds nothing"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:521
msgid "Only published locations with coordinates are searched: open the location and click <strong>Find on map</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:522
msgid "Check the locator’s categories and radius, and the “Limit search to countries” setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:523
msgid "After a direct database import, rebuild the location index (Import & Tools → Maintenance)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:525
msgid "Google Maps shows “For development purposes only”"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:526
msgid "The Google key is missing, restricted to other sites, or billing isn’t enabled in Google Cloud. Without a working key MatrixMap falls back to vector maps."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:527
msgid "A user can’t edit maps or settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:528
msgid "Maps and locations need the “edit_matrixmaps” capabilities (Administrators and Editors have them by default); Settings and Import & Tools need “manage_matrixmap” (Administrators). A role editor plugin can grant them to other roles."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:529
msgid "Emails from forms don’t arrive (Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:530
msgid "Messages, submissions and leads use WordPress email. Many hosts need an SMTP plugin to deliver email reliably; also check the addresses under Settings → Messages, Submissions and Leads to dealers."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:531
msgid "“The routing service is busy” (Pro)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:532
msgid "The open OSRM servers are for light use. For a busy site choose OpenRouteService, GraphHopper, Mapbox or Google with a key (Settings → Directions). Routes are cached, so repeated requests don’t count again."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:544
msgid "Do I need an API key?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:545
msgid "No. Vector maps (the default), classic OpenStreetMap tiles, region maps and the OpenStreetMap address search work without a key. Google Maps and some tile and search providers need one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:546
msgid "What is the difference between Free and Pro?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:547
msgid "The free plugin is complete: maps, store locators, region maps with data, imports and exports, blocks and the Elementor widget, with no limits on maps or locations. Pro adds advanced workflows — directions, submissions and dealer networks, analytics, SEO pages, data sync, drilldown, custom maps, WooCommerce and page-builder integrations. See Pro features."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:548
msgid "What happens if my Pro license expires?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:549
msgid "Pro keeps working. The license brings updates and support."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:550
msgid "I used MatrixMaps 1.x. Will my maps break?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:551
msgid "No. 1.x maps and the <code>[geo_maps]</code> shortcode keep working, and the old data is not deleted."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:552
msgid "Does it work with WPML or Polylang?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:553
msgid "MatrixMap ships a wpml-config.xml so maps and locations can be translated; map labels follow the site language where the map style supports it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:554
msgid "What happens when I uninstall?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:555
msgid "See Security & privacy → Uninstalling. Deactivating never deletes anything."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:567
msgid "What MatrixMap stores"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:569
msgid "Your maps and locations (as WordPress posts), their settings and categories."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:570
msgid "A location index table (coordinates) and an address search cache table, so addresses are looked up only once."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:571
msgid "Plugin settings, including any API keys you enter."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:572
msgid "The free plugin stores nothing about visitors and sets no cookies."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:574
msgid "Outside services"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:575
msgid "A map that shows tiles makes the visitor’s browser download them from the provider you chose (OpenFreeMap by default; OpenStreetMap, Google or another provider if you choose it). That provider receives the visitor’s IP address and browser details, as with any web request — which is why maps can wait for consent. Address searches are made by your server to the search service you chose. Region maps use no outside service."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:578
msgid "<strong>Analytics</strong> is off until you switch it on (MatrixMap → Analytics or Settings → Analytics). It keeps anonymous daily totals only: no cookies and no IP addresses; search areas are rounded to about 11 km."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:579
msgid "<strong>Geo content</strong> shows or hides content by the visitor’s country. When the country can’t be determined it shows the content, so use it for relevance (prices, contacts), never to hide confidential information."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:580
msgid "<strong>Messages and leads</strong> are emailed and not stored on the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:581
msgid "<strong>Submissions</strong> are stored as pending locations with the submitter’s name and email (for the approval email). Only logged-in submitters get a receipt email. A dealer’s enquiry email is stored privately and never shown on the site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:582
msgid "<strong>Directions</strong> send the start and end points to the routing service you chose, through your server; keys stay on the server."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:583
msgid "<strong>IP location database</strong>: downloaded to your server, so visitors’ IP addresses are looked up locally."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:584
msgid "<strong>Click actions</strong> with a video load it from YouTube (privacy-enhanced mode) or Vimeo when the visitor opens it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:586
msgid "Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:587
msgid "Creating and editing maps and locations needs the “edit_matrixmaps” capabilities; settings, imports and exports need “manage_matrixmap”. Public forms (Pro) have spam protection with a hidden field, a minimum fill time and limits per visitor and per site."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:588
msgid "Uninstalling"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:589
msgid "Deactivating keeps everything. Deleting the plugin only stops its scheduled task and keeps your maps, locations and settings, so reinstalling brings everything back."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Docs.php:590
msgid "Only when “Also delete all maps, locations and settings” is on (Settings → Advanced) does deleting the plugin remove all maps, locations and location categories, its settings, capabilities, caches and its own tables. MatrixMap Pro follows the same setting for its own data; its downloaded IP database and licence are always removed with it. This can’t be undone, so export your maps and locations first (Import & Tools)."
msgstr ""

